---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy — AI Crossword Maker"
  description="Refund policy draft for subscriptions and credit packs. Operator entity required before charging cards."
  canonicalPath="/refund-policy/"
>
  <section class="container section prose" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
    <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
    <p>
      <em>
        Draft. Publish final refund terms with a real operator identity before charging cards.
        Do not invent a company name.
      </em>
    </p>

    <h2>Operator</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Legal entity:</strong> [TO BE FILLED BEFORE LAUNCH]<br />
      <strong>Billing support contact:</strong> [TO BE FILLED]
    </p>

    <h2>Intended product behavior (subject to final counsel text)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Subscriptions (Pro monthly/yearly):</strong> cancel anytime via customer portal when
        Stripe is the active provider; access continues through the paid period unless otherwise
        stated in the final policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Credit Packs / Activity Pack:</strong> unused credits may be eligible for refund
        windows defined at launch; consumed AI/export entitlements are generally non-refundable.
      </li>
      <li>
        Chargebacks and disputes follow Stripe/Creem tooling once billing is live.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Publish blocker</h2>
    <p>
      Until the operator entity and support contact are filled, treat this page as incomplete and
      do not rely on it for live payments.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
